# Online Mafia Game - Cursor Rules

> **⚠️ IMPORTANT: Always read `/docs/README.md` before implementing features or fixing bugs.**

## Quick Reference

This is a quick reference. For detailed documentation, see the `/docs` folder:

- **`/docs/README.md`** - Entry point (start here)
- **`/docs/architecture.md`** - Stack, boundaries, data flow
- **`/docs/realtime.md`** - Supabase real-time subscriptions
- **`/docs/game-design.md`** - Mafia rules, phases, visibility
- **`/docs/frontend.md`** - React / UI conventions
- **`/docs/backend.md`** - Server patterns
- **`/docs/decisions.md`** - Architectural decisions (ADR)

## Core Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router)
- **Database & Auth**: Supabase (PostgreSQL + Auth)
- **Real-time**: Supabase Realtime (postgres_changes subscriptions)
- **Video/Audio**: LiveKit (WebRTC)
- **Styling**: TailwindCSS + shadcn/ui
- **Validation**: Zod
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode)

## Key Principles

1. **Server-side authority**: All game logic runs server-side via Next.js Server Actions
2. **Real-time via Supabase**: Use Supabase `postgres_changes` subscriptions for real-time updates
3. **Type safety**: Always use `database.types.ts` for database types, avoid hardcoded types
4. **Component composition**: Break down UIs into small, reusable components
5. **Custom hooks**: Extract data fetching and side effects into hooks under `src/hooks`
6. **Role-based visibility**: Game phase and role determine what players can see (video/UI)

## What We DON'T Use

- ❌ Socket.IO (use Supabase Realtime instead)
- ❌ Redis (use Supabase Realtime instead)
- ❌ Redux/Zustand (use local state + subscriptions)
- ❌ Custom WebRTC (use LiveKit)

## Before Implementing

1. ✅ Read relevant documentation in `/docs`
2. ✅ Check existing patterns in similar features
3. ✅ Use `database.types.ts` types, don't create new ones
4. ✅ Run `npx tsc` after changes to catch type errors
5. ✅ Follow component and hook patterns from existing code

## File Structure

- `/src/app` - Next.js App Router pages
- `/src/components` - React components (organized by feature)
- `/src/hooks` - Custom React hooks
- `/src/lib` - Utility libraries and server actions
- `/src/db/supabase/database.types.ts` - Generated database types (DO NOT EDIT)
- `/src/lib/constants/game.ts` - Game constants (phases, roles, statuses)

## Type Safety

- Always use `Tables<"table_name">` from `database.types.ts`
- Run `npx tsc` after every change
- Avoid `any` types
- Use strict TypeScript

## Real-time Updates

- Use Supabase `postgres_changes` subscriptions
- See existing hooks: `useGameSessionListener`, `useGamePlayerListener`
- Always clean up subscriptions in useEffect return

## Server Actions

- All game logic in server actions (`"use server"`)
- Authenticate first with `supabase.auth.getUser()`
- Use `adminClient` for database writes
- Return `{ ok: true }` or `{ ok: false; message: string }`

## Component Patterns

- Extract logic to custom hooks
- Keep components focused on UI
- Use shadcn/ui components from `/src/components/ui`
- Support dark mode
- Don't define helper functions inside components (use `/src/lib/utils`)

## Game Logic

- Game phases defined in `/src/lib/constants/game.ts`
- Visibility rules in `/src/lib/game/visibility.ts`
- Role filtering in `/src/lib/utils/filterPlayerRoles.ts`
- All phase transitions via server actions
